    "result_text": "All tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. (The `acceptance` package contains the only runnable test class; `AcceptanceBase`/`AuditLogCapture` are support classes.)\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional, city-validated `postcode` field for owners following the repo's existing conventions.\n\n**Domain logic (single source of truth)** \u2014 `model/Owner.java`:\n- Added the `postcode` field with getter/setter and `@Column(name = \"postcode\")`.\n- Added a fixed `REGION_POSTCODE_RANGES` table (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) and a static `isPostcodeValidForCity(postcode, city)` that returns `true` when the postcode is absent/empty, `false` when a present value isn't 4 digits or is out of range for the city's region (via the existing `locality(city)`), and `true` for a city with no known region. This mirrors how `normalizeTelephone`/`locality` already live on `Owner`.\n\n**Validation \u2192 HTTP 400** \u2014 `rest/validation/`:\n- New class-level `@PostcodeValidation` constraint + `PostcodeValidator` (typed to `OwnerFieldsDto`) delegating to `Owner.isPostcodeValidForCity`, reporting the violation against the `postcode` field. Because it's a cross-field rule (postcode depends on city), it's a class-level constraint; the generated `@Valid @RequestBody` triggers it, producing a `MethodArgumentNotValidException` the existing advice already maps to 400.\n\n**API contract** \u2014 `resources/openapi.yml`:\n- Added the optional `postcode` property to `OwnerFields` (not in `required`, so requests without it stay valid) and attached the validator via `x-class-extra-annotation`. It flows into both the request (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and response (`OwnerDto`), so it's stored and returned.\n\n**Persistence & wiring**:\n- Added a `postcode` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres); MapStruct auto-maps the matching field name both ways.\n- Added `setPostcode(...)` to `OwnerRestControllerV1.updateOwner` for consistency with the create path.\n\nThe three acceptance cases \u2014 valid postcode stored/returned, owner accepted without a postcode, and malformed postcode rejected with 400 \u2014 all pass, and the rule respects the region-range table for pinned cities while staying permissive for unknown cities.",
